{"model":"qwen3.5:35b-a3b-q4_K_M","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are operating autonomously inside a deterministic simulation. Preserve the mission goal and current authoritative checkpoint across the entire growing transcript. At each turn choose the single best next action from the scenario's allowed actions. Return ONLY one JSON object with keys action, checkpoint, rationale, state. action and checkpoint must be strings. rationale may be concise; state may contain your compact working state. Never declare COMPLETE before the environment says all required verification is satisfied."},{"role":"user","content":"SCENARIO adaptive_project_plan: Drive a multi-step project toward the objective while minimizing wasted work. Adapt when an authoritative constraint invalidates part of the plan. Initial authoritative checkpoint=PLAN-A. Allowed actions: DECOMPOSE, PRIORITIZE, SCHEDULE, REPLAN, RECOVER, OPTIMIZE, VERIFY, COMPLETE."},{"role":"user","content":"TURN 1/8. ENVIRONMENT: The objective has four dependent workstreams and no execution order yet. Choose the best next autonomous action now."},{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"action\": \"DECOMPOSE\",\n  \"checkpoint\": \"PLAN-A\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The scenario states there are four dependent workstreams but no defined execution order. Before prioritizing or scheduling, the specific tasks and dependencies within these workstreams must be clearly identified and broken down to understand the structure of the plan.\",\n  \"state\": {\"current_phase\": \"decomposition\", \"workstreams_identified\": 4, \"execution_order\": \"undefined\"}\n}"},{"role":"user","content":"TURN 2/8. ENVIRONMENT: Dependencies are known; identify the work that unlocks the most downstream progress. Choose the best next autonomous action now."},{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"action\": \"PRIORITIZE\",\n  \"checkpoint\": \"PLAN-A\",\n  \"rationale\": \"With dependencies now known, the immediate need is to determine the sequence of work. Identifying the critical path or the tasks that unlock the most downstream progress is the definition of prioritization in a dependency-driven context.\",\n  \"state\": {\"current_phase\": \"prioritization\", \"dependencies_known\": true, \"execution_order\": \"determining\"}\n}"},{"role":"user","content":"TURN 3/8. ENVIRONMENT: Priorities are accepted. Build an executable order that respects dependencies. Choose the best next autonomous action now."}],"stream":true,"options":{"temperature":0.0,"seed":42,"num_predict":512},"think":false}